<title>GERMANY: Buba allots 69.1 bln marks in tender at 3.00 pct.</title>
<headline>Buba allots 69.1 bln marks in tender at 3.00 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Wednesday that it allocated securities repurchase funds at this week's tender at a fixed rate of 3.00 percent.</p>
<p>The German central bank accepted bids for 69.1 billion marks of the 13-day funds. A repo pact for 68.9 billion marks expires today, Wednesday, so a net 200 million marks is flowing into the market.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank said banks bid for 196.1 billion marks of the repurchase funds this week. It accepted 35.25 percent of the bids made.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
